! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Natural World", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Animal World", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking for Clarification and Emphasizing a Point", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want more information from someone, you can use <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span>. <br/><br/>You can emphasize a point by asking <span class=\"strong\">rhetorical questions</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Embedded questions</span> are questions within other questions or statements. Often, you use the phrases <span class=\"italic\">Do you know ... </span>, <span class=\"italic\">Do you remember ... </span>, <span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me ...</span>  or <span class=\"italic\">Can you show me ...</span> to start an <span class=\"strong\">embedded question</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For Example:<br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Direct question</span>: <span class=\"italic\">What are you trying to say?</span><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Embedded question</span>: <span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me what you are trying to say?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can emphasize a point by using rhetorical questions which are questions that don't need to be answered. They are said when the speaker wants to express their feelings about a situation. The speaker does not expect the listener to actually give an answer. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  For example: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What are you going to do? </span>(when there is nothing to be done) <br/><span class=\"italic\">How about that?</span> (when you want to make a point)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Can you clarify what you're trying to say?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm not sure what you're trying to tell me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How's that working for you?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to forward", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to send an e-mail to a further destination", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I forwarded you an online brochure I got the other day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about nature.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Showing That You Understand Someone's Feelings", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In conversation, one way to keep the conversation going is to show empathy. This means showing that you understand the other person's feelings or situation. You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> followed by an adjective when you want to empathize with someone. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> and an adjective (either in it's ED or ING form). When you use the -ED form, it refers to the feelings that a person has. When you use the -ING form, it refers to the thing that is causing feelings.<br/><br/>For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">You must be delighted.<br/> You must be nervous.<br/> They must be surprised!<br/> It must be terrifying to do that!<br/><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your work must be exciting!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You must be bored with your job right now.", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "offender ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a person who commits a crime", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our officers make sure that that offenders cannot avoid punishment by simply crossing into another country.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to endeavor", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to try hard to do or achieve something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Wildlife enforcement officers endeavor to protect those plant and animal species which are threatened again and again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "illicit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "illegal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nations work together to control the illicit trade of endangered species. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "migratory", "type": "name"}, {"content": " referring to an animal that migrates (changes its habitat based on climate)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One illegal act is poaching migratory birds.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to traffic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move illegally for money", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Another illegal act is killing or trafficking endangered species.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "career path", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the way that you progress in your work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Find me another career path!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Design a PSA with your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose a topic that you both feel is important.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a short announcement about it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read it to another group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your opinions and feelings about each other's topics.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a short PSA about a topic of interest.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the PSA with another group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss my opinions and feelings about various topics.", "type": "text"}]}]}